Conclusion
The College Attendance Management System must balance the needs of students, teachers, and management. By identifying clear requirements, prioritizing them with the MoSCoW technique, classifying features using the Kano Model, and resolving stakeholder conflicts through negotiation and phased implementation, the project can deliver a practical, cost-effective, and user-focused attendance system while meeting both technical and business objectives.



